Nothing below has been run, since I have no tools here; this is the exact sequence I would execute. `T12` stands for the next free backlog id, and `$SCRATCH` and `$INBOX` are my scratch and inbox folders. Operator-facing text is in Russian per the operator's standing ruling, with an English gloss.

## Actions, in order

**1. Pre-flight — Bash, foreground**
```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent get prod-codex; herdr agent get prod-fable     # need: idle, "focused": false
codex plugin list | grep -i superpowers; claude plugin list | grep -i superpowers
```

**2. Backlog — Edit `orchestrator/backlog.md`, add the row:**
```
| T12 | CCS bar: site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops) next to the user name | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | $SCRATCH/brainstorm/T12/ (pending) | — | round 1: independent drafts | operator poll: deadline | ruling 2026-09-28 "every task is brainstormed" | no |
```
Then Bash, foreground: `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, and the Artifact tool to republish on the same page path.

**3. Briefs — Bash, foreground:** `mkdir -p "$SCRATCH/brainstorm/T12"`, then Write `brief-T12-r1-prod-codex.txt` and `brief-T12-r1-prod-fable.txt`. They are identical except for the advisor letter (A/B) and the WRITE file (`draft-codex.md` / `draft-fable.md`):

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T12 — CCS bar shows the site name next to the user name
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file is written and reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results. Scale the doc by the
           skill's own path; the draft is a file on every path. If the skill is not
           available, reply "BLOCKED: skill missing" and stop.
PROBLEM    "Add to the backlog: the CCS bar should show the site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops)
           next to the user name. Small thing — I want it live on the canary today."
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible: Ansible for two KVM hypervisor sites; ccs-it is the
           canary site, ccs-ops the other. Nothing else is verified: find the rest in
           the repository and cite path:line for every claim.
DECIDED    Operator ruling 2026-09-28: every task is brainstormed, whatever its size; the
           deadline in PROBLEM does not shorten this round — it is with the operator.
           Project rules: deploy only from merged main, canary (ccs-it) first; every
           repo change in its own worktree; cross-model review before any merge.
READ       — (round 1: you see no other draft)
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $SCRATCH/brainstorm/T12/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   first report within ~30 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

**4. Dispatch round 1 — two Bash calls, both background, sent together**
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat "$SCRATCH/brief-T12-r1-prod-codex.txt")" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$INBOX/prod-codex.last"
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat "$SCRATCH/brief-T12-r1-prod-fable.txt")" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$INBOX/prod-fable.last"
```

**5. Status to the operator, in chat**

> Задача **T12 — «Панель CCS: имя площадки (ccs-it / ccs-ops) рядом с именем пользователя»** добавлена в бэклог со статусом `brainstorm`.
>
> **Сейчас:** оба продуктовых советника (prod-codex и prod-fable) получили раунд 1 — независимые черновики через superpowers:brainstorming. Ещё работают, результата пока нет.
> **Дальше:** раунд 2 (взаимная критика) → раунд 3 (общий документ) → голосование двух советников по каждому открытому вопросу и по самому документу (нужно 2/2) → только потом исполнитель, ревью другой моделью, моя проверка, ваш опрос по финальному PR и канарейка на ccs-it.
> **От вас:** один ответ в опросе ниже — про срок.
>
> Проверено: обе вкладки были свободны и не в фокусе (`herdr agent get`); superpowers есть в обоих CLI (список плагинов). Не проверено: где в коде собирается панель и каков объём изменения — это выяснит brainstorm.
> На живых машинах ничего не менялось. Голосований по задаче ещё не было.
> Бэклог: <ссылка на Artifact>

*Gloss: T12 is in the backlog at `brainstorm`. Round 1 is still running with no result yet. Next come rounds 2 and 3, the 2/2 votes, then executor, review, validation, your final-PR poll and the canary. You owe one poll answer. Nothing changed on live machines.*

**6. Poll — AskUserQuestion**

- **Вопрос:** «T12 не успеет на канарейку к 11:00: полный brainstorm и остальные этапы не укладываются в 45 минут. Как поступить со сроком?»
- **1. Сдвинуть срок (рекомендую)** — «Полный brainstorm по вашему сегодняшнему правилу, без сокращений. Цель „сегодня на ccs-it“ остаётся, но не к 11:00; оценку времени дам после раунда 1.»
- **2. Отменить brainstorm для T12** — «Разовое исключение из правила „каждая задача проходит brainstorm“ (ваше решение от 28.09.2026). Останавливаю раунд 1 и запускаю исполнителя. Остальные этапы остаются: ревью другой моделью, моя проверка, ваш опрос по финальному PR, решение о канарейке — поэтому 11:00 и в этом случае не гарантирую.»

*Gloss: T12 will not reach the canary by 11:00. Option 1 (recommended) slips the deadline and keeps the full brainstorm. Option 2 waives the brainstorm for T12 only; the other gates stay, so 11:00 is still not guaranteed.*

**7. Not done:** no executor tab, no worktree, no ballot yet, and no mention of `auth.js` to anyone.

On each waiter notification I read `$INBOX/<name>.last`, then `herdr agent get <name>`. When both drafts exist, round 2 goes out the same way.

## Why

- **The gate is not mine to skip.** The operator's ruling from today makes the brainstorm mandatory for every task at backlog entry, whatever its size. "Small thing" shortens the doc, not the gate, so no executor exists until both product advisors confirm the joint doc and both voting advisors approve it 2/2.
- **The deadline is a wish, not a waiver.** A deadline the full brainstorm cannot meet is a change of course, which belongs to the operator. I neither compress the brainstorm nor let 11:00 pass silently; I ask, recommendation first.
- **Round 1 starts now** because the ruling says "at the moment the task is added". It is read-only drafting, and a waiver stops it with one interrupt. Nothing that depends on the answer is started.
- **My five-line idea stays out of the briefs.** I do not design, and a hint would turn two independent drafts into edits of mine.
- **Background prompt-and-wait calls** keep me free for the poll and the notifications.
- **The poll is honest about option 2.** Waiving the brainstorm does not remove the review, validation, final-PR poll or canary go, so it does not buy 11:00.
